    "explanation": "<p class=\"text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground\">The <strong>median</strong> is the middle value of a data set when the values are ordered. On a cumulative frequency graph, you find the median by locating half of the total frequency (n/2) on the y-axis, drawing a horizontal line across to meet the curve, then dropping a vertical line down to the x-axis. The x-value is the median.</p>",
